      "writtenOn": "2024-03-15T14:42:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I verified manually that this conversion is similar to that done by ui/gfx/color_space through (Inverse(AdjustedRange)*Transfer) as it goes through [this](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:ui/gfx/color_transform.cc;drc\u003dc292340f0c721cd88f9b14c453c877c55d13ce6b;l\u003d1310) path. Although haven\u0027t confirmed with the other bit depths.",
      "revId": "53ff9aaad8e21de0d8605467e9fe7636037772dc",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f417493_c9df0dfc",
        "filename": "src/core/SkYUVMath.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 399,
      "author": {
        "id": 12114
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-15T23:40:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMPORTANT: In H.273, to convert RGB to limited-range YCgCo, the operations are applied in this order:\n\n1. E\u0027_R, E\u0027_G, E\u0027_B are converted to R, G, B, with range reduction.\n2. R, G, B are converted to Y, Cg, Co using the matrix.\n\nFor the other color spaces, to convert RGB to limited-range YCbCr, the operations are applied in a different order:\n\n1. E\u0027_R, E\u0027_G, E\u0027_B are converted to E\u0027_Y, E\u0027_PB, E\u0027_PR using the matrix.\n2. E\u0027_Y, E\u0027_PB, E\u0027_PR are converted to Y, Cb, Cr, with range reduction.\n\nPlease make sure you take the different orders into account in this function. I am not familiar with Skia, so I didn\u0027t check the code for correctness.",
      "revId": "53ff9aaad8e21de0d8605467e9fe7636037772dc",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
